+idp#514 by hand; `helm-retry` resets every Failed HelmRelease with `flux reconcile --reset`; `dns-per-node` runs an in-cluster and an external nslookup pinned to every node; `dns-per-namespace` resolves every headless Service of each not-Ready namespace from a probe inside it and lists its EndpointSlices; `tcp-per-node` connects from a probe inside each not-Ready namespace, pinned to every node, to every ClusterIP Service port of that namespace and prints the reachable matrix; `node-drain` cordons and drains the Ready node carrying the most not-Running pods so the autoscaler replaces it, `node-uncordon` is its undo), and applies the original list again from an `EXIT` trap, so a failed playbook
 never leaves the door open. The job log is the receipt: `admit-apply`, the playbook's step lines,
 `revoke-apply`. Nothing is typed ad hoc: a new playbook is a reviewed function in the script and a
 name in the workflow's `playbook` choice.
